/-!
# VIII09 — the actual ε³ Maxwell bridge

For fixed `R > 3` the frozen residual along the test family

  `f_ε = f0 (1 + ε² u)`, `m_ε = m0 (1 + ε² z)`, `N_ε = N`, `a_ε = ε b1 + ε³ c`,
  `J_ε = ε j`

is a polynomial in `ε` with **no** constant, linear, or `ε²` term.  Writing

  `A1 = m0 D1 - f0 b1 - C (j + 2Q b1)`
  `A3 = m0 (z D1 + D3) - f0 (u b1 + c) - C (2Q c + (u + 2z)(j + 2Q b1))`

with `C = 2Q f0 m0²/N²`, `D1 = (m0 b1')'`, `D3 = (m0 (z b1' + c'))'`, the `ε`-linear coefficient
`A1` vanishes because `b1 = b*` solves the first-order magnetic equation, so the residual is
`ε³ (A3 + O(ε²))`.  Then `A3 = P·(Lmag c - q3_j(1/R)/R³)` exactly — the compact source enters
only through its definition, not by substitution.
-/

